WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:02.410
Speaker 1: Let's go to James from Southern
California.

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:03.669
James from Southern California.

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:05.020
Welcome to the program.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.730
What is on your mind today, sir?

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.050
Speaker 4: Thank you very much.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.230
David, are you able to hear me okay?

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.639
Speaker 1: I can hear you beautifully.

00:00:10.639 --> 00:00:13.841
Speaker 4: I want to start by thanking you
for everything you do.

00:00:13.841 --> 00:00:19.180
I really appreciate all you've done over the
years on your program.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.789
I have a comment and I have a question.

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:22.869
Sure.

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:29.340
One comment I want to make regarding the people
with the MAGA mentality.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.660
I really want to encourage everyone to be
patient with these folks because we can get

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.660
through to them.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.660
I've had a lot of success.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:42.660
And I think the approach I use is very important
in remembering that they do live in fear to

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.570
some extent, very much happen to us in their
mentality.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:47.570
Oh, yeah.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.220
And if you can establish that you are one
of them and we are us.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.199
They will listen to you.

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:56.050
And as long as you don't tell them they're
wrong, but simply give them information, but

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:01.750
build from the bottom up, remembering that
they're ignorant like little children.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.470
And you need to use terms and concepts.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:09.950
And once you have them on your side and they're
agreeing with you, you can start correcting

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:15.020
the misinformation that's in their head and
help them kind of re build their view of reality.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.120
Speaker 1: I don't disagree with that one
bit.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.580
Speaker 4: It takes a lot of patience.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:20.580
Yes.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.950
And I really want to encourage people to go
out to friends, family members who are frustrating

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:28.320
you and try to approach them as they are a
little child.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.090
Speaker 1: Well, here's the thing, James.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.600
Everything you're saying is correct.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:38.409
The important thing to remember is that's
like a retail strategy person by person.

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:40.950
And it's insanely time consuming.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.960
Doesn't mean we don't do it, but it is insanely
time consuming.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:50.170
We also want to see, is there some wholesale
approach that might deprogram larger numbers

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:51.430
of these people?

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.189
And that's a tougher question to answer.

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:55.180
Speaker 4: It is indeed.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:59.969
But I believe we need to approach this from
the grassroots because we all have a friend

00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:02.390
or family member that we are probably avoiding.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.789
Instead, we need to help them, right?

00:02:04.789 --> 00:02:06.159
We need to help our community.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.570
And I think it's a big part.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:08.570
It's on us.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.729
Rather than letting it happen.

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:11.729
We need to be patient.

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:13.560
Speaker 3: And take the time.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.569
And yes, it is time consuming, but it does
work.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.790
Speaker 4: It can be done.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:21.890
I have faith in that and I just wanted to
make that comment fair because many of us

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.800
are feeling a little hopeless.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.230
But don't give up on it, you know, take that
stand.

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:28.629
Anyway, I have a question for you.

00:02:28.629 --> 00:02:29.629
Sure.

00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:35.300
I was wondering, what do you think the odds
are of Tucker Carlson ending up on Newsmax?

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.700
Speaker 1: That's a good question.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.920
You know, I have I have no idea.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.920
I don't think I have anything substantive
or objective that I could say.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.900
Could Tucker Carlson end up on Newsmax?

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:50.930
I know the CEO of Newsmax, interestingly enough,
he's kind of like a fan of my work.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:55.330
Interestingly, even though our political views
are very, very different.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:57.920
He is at heart a business person.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:03.250
And so without a doubt, if I had to bet, I
would bet that he's looking to see what could

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:06.200
happen, maybe with Tucker Carlson on Newsmax.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:13.590
My instinct is that it would be neither prestigious
nor lucrative enough for Tucker Carlson to

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:14.590
join.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:20.370
I think Tucker Carlson would have more to
gain from launching his own thing from scratch.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.480
But it's not impossible.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.390
I don't know where Tucker is going to end
up.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.510
Speaker 4: Yeah, I don't either.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:27.590
I'm worried about that.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.819
I was just wondering about your take on that.

00:03:29.819 --> 00:03:31.239
Well, thank you so much, David.

00:03:31.239 --> 00:03:33.200
I really appreciate everything you do for
us.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.200
Speaker 1: My pleasure.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.060
James from Southern California.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.340
